    "result_text": "All 262 tests pass \u2014 `BUILD SUCCESS`. (The `ERROR ExceptionControllerAdvice` line is a deliberate negative-path assertion in `UserRestControllerV1Tests`, which itself reports 0 failures.)\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented the immutable structured `OWNER_CREATED` audit event as specified.\n\n**New file \u2014 `audit/OwnerCreatedEvent.java`:** an immutable class (all fields `final`, no setters) holding `seq`, `ownerId`, the owner's **current primary identifier**, and `membershipLevel`. Its `toJson()` renders a compact JSON object with a stable field order `{seq, ownerId, customerCode, membershipLevel, event:\"OWNER_CREATED\"}` via Jackson. The identifier is stored as a generic \"primary identifier\" value published under the `customerCode` key today \u2014 so when the customerCode is later unified into the memberId, the call site just passes the memberId and only this one key name changes.\n\n**`OwnerRestControllerV1.java`:**\n- Added a static `AtomicLong CREATE_SEQUENCE` for a monotonically increasing sequence across creates.\n- After the existing human-readable audit line (kept intact), it emits the structured event via the same `AUDIT` logger, incrementing the sequence once per successful create and passing the owner's current `customerCode` as the primary identifier.\n\nEmitted output confirmed in the run:\n```\nAUDIT - {\"seq\":1,\"ownerId\":11,\"customerCode\":\"NSW-16E6609E\",\"membershipLevel\":1,\"event\":\"OWNER_CREATED\"}\n```\n\nThe `AcceptanceTest.coreEventCarriesIdAndIdentifier` check (event line containing the marker, owner id, and customerCode) passes, and no existing tests regressed.",
